    <!-- What each home layout is like (side panel). -->
    <string name="look_layout_shelves_help">Rows you scroll through: continue playing, systems, collections and your apps. Tandem\'s classic home.</string>
    <string name="look_layout_grid_help">Every system, folder, app and game as a square icon on one dense grid that scrolls sideways, with a pill dock. The other screen shows the highlighted icon big; X swaps the screens.</string>
    <string name="look_layout_carousel_help">A coverflow: the highlighted card sits big in the middle and the others turn away to the sides.</string>
    <string name="look_layout_list_help">Compact rows with a big preview beside them. Fast to scan, great for huge libraries.</string>
    <string name="look_layout_console_help">A console-style dashboard: the highlighted item\'s art fills the screen with one row of big tiles along the bottom.</string>
    <string name="look_layout_orbit_help">Tandem\'s own: your systems, collections and apps ride a glowing ring of glassy orbs, the highlighted one big at the front. Inside the ring its latest games stand as a row of covers, the Continue card beside them. Left and Right spin it, L1 and R1 jump between groups, X swaps the screens.</string>
    <string name="look_layout_spotlight_help">Game first: the highlighted game\'s art fills the screen, a rail of covers runs down one side and its logo, story and play time sit on the other. Up and Down move the rail, L1 and R1 change system or collection, X reads the whole story.</string>

